                "reply_count": 4,
                "retweet_count": 12,
                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "This Administration has created a health care crisis for South Texas, leaving folks like Alix Flores of Brownsville to suffer.\n\nWithout expanded ACA tax credits, Mr. Flores' monthly health insurance will spike from $12 to $275. And if forced off insurance, he'll pay nearly $1,000 out of pocket for medication to manage a chronic illness.\n\nMr. Flores and the 142,000 South Texans in our district who are about to see their premiums skyrocket deserve better. Congress can and must immediately extend ACA tax credits.",
